The fabric routes all leaf-to-leaf traffic through `spine_router_0_1` only — due to the "Older Path" BGP tiebreaker (FRR keeps whichever equal-cost path was learned first, because `bgp bestpath compare-routerid` is not configured and `maximum-paths` is absent). `spine_router_0_0` holds the alternate paths in its BGP table but never wins selection. This is a configuration optimisation gap (no ECMP, non-deterministic spine selection), **not a fault causing loss** — backup failover to `spine_router_0_0` would work if `spine_router_0_1` dropped.

