=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported end-to-end outage between pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) and pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2)
is not substantiated by any evidence in the live lab. Direct ping from pc_0_0 to
pc_0_1 completes with 4/4 packets and zero loss, and a full traceroute confirms a
clean 4-hop path: pc_0_0 → leaf_router_0_0 → spine_router_0_1 → leaf_router_0_1
→ pc_0_1. Host IP addresses and default gateways match the ticket exactly (both
PCs configured correctly). All five FRR routers have their BGP sessions established,
all physical interfaces on both spines are UP, and each device has correct forwarding
entries for both 10.0.0.0/24 and 10.0.1.0/24. The team's hypothesis of a cable
failure between rack switches is incorrect — no link is down.

One observation worth noting: the fabric is not ECMP-balanced. Because
bgp bestpath compare-routerid and maximum-paths are absent from every router's
BGP config, FRR resolves ties with the non-deterministic "Older Path" rule and
installs only a single best path. As a result, spine_router_0_1 is universally
preferred (it advertised first on lab startup) and spine_router_0_0 carries no
data-plane traffic, though it holds warm backup paths that would activate after
BGP reconvergence if spine_router_0_1 failed. This is a configuration gap — not
a fault. Corrective action: add bgp bestpath compare-routerid and maximum-paths 2
under router bgp on all five devices to restore deterministic, load-balanced Clos
behaviour. The user's connectivity complaint appears to be a false premise; the
network has been reachable throughout.
=== END ===
